    "updated_at": "2018-02-24T17:20:04Z",
    "body": "I think the list is a decent bit longer than that; in particular anything with an invalid value default.\r\n\r\nI'd prefer to be able to leave basic HTML syntax questions in a dedicated section, and not re-explain them in every attribute where they're relevant. Where does it end? Explaining that you don't need to use quotes around attributes for all attributes whose values don't usually contain spaces or other special characters? Explaining for every element that attributes are case-insensitive (when set by the parser)?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
